/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 700 Tm (The same argument applies to long form reading. A person who wants to hear a) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 684 Tm (two hundred page report while walking the dog is not asking for a summary.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 668 Tm (They are asking for the whole thing, spoken at a steady pace, with the) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 652 Tm (paragraph breaks preserved and the footnotes skipped. Doing this well is) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 636 Tm (mostly a text processing problem. A PDF is a container for positioned glyphs,) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 620 Tm (not for sentences, so the pipeline must reconstruct the sentences first:) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 604 Tm (remove the running head, drop the page numbers, undo the hyphenation that) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 588 Tm (the typesetter inserted to justify a line, then cut the result into chunks) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 572 Tm (that a speech model can handle without losing the thread of the argument.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 540 Tm (There is a second reason to keep the model small. Synthesis at a hundred) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 524 Tm (times real time means a one hour audiobook renders in under a minute, which) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 508 Tm (makes batch generation practical on a laptop. A publisher can produce six) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 492 Tm (voice variants of the same chapter, listen to all of them, and keep the one) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 476 Tm (that sounds least like a machine reading a telephone directory.) Tj
